    "sections": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Coraline revolutionized stop-motion animation with its haunting portrayal of childhood fears. Director Henry Selick crafted a dark fantasy masterpiece that builds on his work in <a href=\"/movie/9479\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"9479\">The Nightmare Before Christmas</a> (1993), pushing technical boundaries with intricate handmade puppets and sets. The film's signature blue-haired heroine navigates between worlds through a mysterious door, echoing classic portal fantasies like <a href=\"/movie/1417\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"1417\">Pan's Labyrinth</a> (2006) but with a distinctly modern American gothic twist. The button-eyed Other Mother stands among animation's most terrifying villains, drawing from psychological horror traditions seen in <a href=\"/movie/242224\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"242224\">The Babadook</a> (2014)."
      },
      {
