            "tmdb_id": 9297,
            "poster_url": "https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/zCRPr4bkO3ae0U1134vJ39xZnAG.jpg"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Coraline paved the way for more sophisticated children's horror, inspiring films like <a href=\"/movie/62214\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"62214\">Frankenweenie</a> (2012) and <a href=\"/movie/170687\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"170687\">The Boxtrolls</a> (2014). Its success proved audiences would embrace darker themes in animation, leading to more complex works like <a href=\"/movie/110420\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"110420\">Wolf Children</a> (2012) and <a href=\"/movie/110416\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"110416\">Song of the Sea</a> (2014). The film's exploration of parallel worlds and maternal relationships echoes through modern animation, from <a href=\"/movie/150540\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"150540\">Inside Out</a> (2015) to The Mitchell's vs. The Machines (2021)."
      }
